    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (6 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nI moved the date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 so 1 July 2025\u201330 June 2026 is FY26).\n\n**New single-responsibility class \u2014 `model/FiscalYear.java`**\nThe one home for the fiscal-year rule. It exposes exactly three derivations:\n- `of(date)` \u2192 the fiscal-year number,\n- `label(date)` \u2192 `\"FY<YY>\"`,\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2192 elapsed fiscal years (difference of fiscal-year numbers).\n\nEverything date-derived now delegates here instead of re-deriving the 1-July boundary in three places.\n\n**Reused it in the three affected spots:**\n1. `MembershipNumber.of` \u2014 the `M<YY>` segment now uses `FiscalYear.of(registrationDate)` instead of the calendar year.\n2. `MembershipLevel` \u2014 tenure now counts elapsed fiscal years: `TENURE_DAYS = 365`/`ChronoUnit.DAYS` replaced by `TENURE_FISCAL_YEARS = 1` and `FiscalYear.elapsed(...) >= 1`. A newly created owner still has 0 elapsed fiscal years, preserving the \"no tenure points at creation\" invariant.\n3. `OwnerMapper` \u2014 new `fiscalYear(owner)` mapping returning `FiscalYear.label(...)`, wired to the new `fiscalYear` response field.\n\n**Schema (`openapi.yml`, source of the generated `OwnerDto`):** added the `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`, `readOnly`) and updated the `membershipNumber` / `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nBoth the membership number and `fiscalYear` read from the same registration date, which the pipeline has already rolled to a business day (`RollRegistrationDateToBusinessDay` runs before the responders), so both are naturally business-day-adjusted with no extra wiring.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec didn't pin the exact tenure threshold, so I translated \"exceeds 365 days\" to \"at least one elapsed fiscal year\" (`>= TENURE_FISCAL_YEARS`, = 1). If you intended stricter (a full fiscal year strictly beyond the first, i.e. `> 1`), that's a one-line change to the constant/comparison.",
